   "determination_full": "NOT-YET on 2026-08-04-nyiso-120-c119-scope, RE-VERIFIED 2026-08-04 without a solve (scripts/calibration_verdict.py --run-id, committed artifacts only, rule 22 D-5(b)). THIS IS A WORSE DETERMINATION THAN THE SUPERSEDED 2026-08-03-nyiso-119-seny-increment CARRIED, AND IT IS WRITTEN ONLY BECAUSE THE OWNER RULED ON IT. D-5(b) requires that a worse re-verified determination STOP the promotion and escalate rather than be silently written; it was escalated with the full numbers and the owner ruled PROMOTE. WHAT CHANGED: C3a mean LMP FAILS on 2025 at -10.1 % against the +/-10 % band, where the same-HEAD control reads -9.5 % PASS. Every other criterion is unchanged: C1 14/14 all and 10/10 free in BOTH arms, C2, C3b, C4, C6, C7, C8 PASS, and C3c remains the single ledgered caveat. 2023 IMPROVES (+7.6 % -> +7.2 %) and 2024 stays inside band (-0.5 % -> -0.9 %); the 2025 move is worth -$0.38/MWh on a $60 mean against a $6.68/MWh gap, so the correction accounts for ~6 % of that gap and ~94 % is pre-existing. WHY THE TRADE WAS ACCEPTED: the promoted run lands a measured INPUT correction with zero free parameters -- eGRID's CHP credit at ORIS 2493 East River is the plant's direct-fired BOILER fuel, not a topping-cycle steam credit, established by two independent meters agreeing to 1.0 % and 0.6 %, so the incumbent add-back was double-counting boiler fuel into a 306 MW NYC CT_CHP tranche and pricing it 59 % above what the machine burns. Rules 1 [R-STRUCT] and 14 [R-ACCURATE] forbid reverting an accurate input because a residual moved the wrong way, and the adverse-gate case was pre-registered in advance. THE LEDGERED-CAVEAT BUDGET IS UNSPENT BY THIS CHANGE: 1 of 3, unchanged. The C3a FAIL is a criterion failure, NOT a new ledger entry, and is deliberately not ledgered -- it is an open residual for NYISO's next session, whose named object is the 2025 under-pricing this correction did not create. NOTE ON PHRASING: the superseded run's own determination token is deliberately NOT spelled out in this field. audit_keepers M1b extracts the FIRST determination token appearing anywhere in this prose and re-verifies it against the run the entry names, so naming a second run's status here would make the marker assert a determination that was never scored against 2026-08-04-nyiso-120-c119-scope -- exactly the silent transfer D-5(b) exists to prevent. The superseded determination is recorded in the keeper shard's promotion_note and in docs/calibration-log/nyiso.md."
